--recurse
# Integration tests each boot their own ephemeral dev server and drive real
# RPCs against it. Running them concurrently with the parallel unit/replay
# phase starves the worker on a small box, so a dev-server RPC, connect, or
# shutdown intermittently trips a deadline (the P10.0 flakes). Fix: split the
# run into two phases. Unit, replay, and the load test are matched to `par`
# rules and run in parallel. The integration tests are matched by NO rule, so
# per prove's resolution ("any test which does not match a rule will be run in
# sequence at the end of the run") they run one at a time AFTER the parallel
# phase drains -- on an otherwise-idle box, with full CPU for the dev server
# and worker. The command stays `prove -lj4 t`; only the schedule changes.
--rules=par=t/unit/*.t
--rules=par=t/replay/*.t
--rules=par=t/00-load.t
